# Trivy CVE allowlist. AGENTS.md policy: each entry needs a rationale + review-by date.
# When the upstream fix lands (or the review-by date arrives), audit and remove.

# Three sharp advisories, all in native libraries sharp bundles:
# GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj (HIGH): libvips CVEs (CVE-2026-33327, CVE-2026-33328,
#   CVE-2026-35590, CVE-2026-35591), fixed in 0.35.0.
#   https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
# GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c (HIGH): libheif (GHSA-g89c-p67h-r497, GHSA-2jg2-4ch7-h545),
#   fixed in 0.35.4.
#   https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c
# GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w (HIGH): librsvg (CVE-2026-96889), fixed in 0.35.5.
#   https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w
# Our direct sharp is 0.35.5 (patched against all three). The flagged copies are
# dev/build-only transitives: 0.34.5 (miniflare, the local dev runtime under wrangler
# and @cloudflare/vite-plugin) and 0.33.5 (favilib via astro-favicons, build-time
# favicon generation). Neither reaches the workerd production runtime. Both are
# pinned by their parents (miniflare exactly, favilib to the 0.33 line), and neither
# line has a patched release, so a caret override cannot dedupe them and forcing
# 0.35.x under them risks breaking native bindings.
# Re-checked 2026-10-22: favilib's last release is still 1.0.5 on ^0.33.5; the
# newest wrangler moves to a pre-release miniflare 5 that takes sharp 0.35.5.
# Review-by: 2026-12-15 (drop once miniflare and favilib ship sharp >= 0.35.5).
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c
GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w
